    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`search_products` is implemented in `solution.py`, and the 17 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates, so those results are unknown.\n\n- **Query:** it is parameterised and picks one of four fixed ORDER BY statements. `order_by` never gets spliced into the SQL text. The ORDER BY always ends with `id ASC`, so ties break by id whichever way `descending` goes.\n- **Search text:** `%`, `_` and backslash in `name_contains` are escaped, so they match literally. The query only reads, so it never modifies the database.\n- **Validation:** `order_by`, `limit` and `offset` are checked up front and raise `ValueError` when invalid. The spec doesn't mention booleans, so I also reject `True` and `False` for `limit` and `offset`.\n- **Tests:** they cover the stock filter, case-insensitive matching, literal wildcards, `max_price` at its boundary, all four orderings, `limit` and `offset`, invalid inputs and that the database is left unchanged.",
